es.  \n","   - Corregir tipos de variables.  \n","3. **Construcción de datos**  \n","   - Transformar formatos (pivotar, normalizar, etc.).  \n","4. **Integración de datos**  \n","   - Alinear índices y preparar para el merge posterior.  \n","5. **Formateo final**  \n","   - Verificar shapes y valores faltantes.\n","\n","Cada dataset se tratará de forma independiente siguiendo estas subfases.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"kayMetYOrfZj"},"source":["# Cell: Limpieza y preparación independiente de cada dataset\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":75,"status":"ok","timestamp":1747228584787,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"},"user_tz":300},"id":"qEgbL2QpmXyE","outputId":"e60dd0f6-18af-46eb-8c7e-fe925f5d23f7"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Antes: (289003, 2) aristas\n","Después: (289003, 2) aristas limpias\n"]}],"source":["# 1) edges_df: eliminar duplicados, self-loops y verificar tipos\n","edges_df = pd.read_csv('musae_git_edges.csv', names=['id_1','id_2'], header=0)\n","print(f\"Antes: {edges_df.shape} aristas\")\n","edges_df = edges_df.drop_duplicates()\n","edges_df = edges_df[edges_df['id_1'] != edges_df['id_2']]  # quitar self-loops\n","edges_df = edges_df.astype(int)\n","print(f\"Después: {edges_df.shape} aristas limpias\")\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"eA8Rz4PVriOC"},"outputs":[],"source":[]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":352,"status":"ok","timestamp":1747228585177,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"},"user_tz":300},"id":"nivUwW3dmmTN","outputId":"d1b4318c-493d-477c-e83f-8e32b4c63ad5"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Antes: (690374, 2) filas de features\n","Después: (37700, 42) (nodos × dimensiones)\n"]}],"source":["# 2) features_df: pivotar para obtener embedding por nodo\n","features_df = pd.read_csv('musae_git_features.csv')\n","print(f\"Antes: {features_df.shape} filas de features\")\n","# Suponemos que 'feature' es una dimensión de embedding indexada por posición\n","features_wide = (\n","    features_df\n","    .assign(dim=lambda df: df.groupby('node').cumcount())\n","    .pivot(index='node', columns='dim', values='feature')\n","    .fillna(0)\n",")\n","features_wide.columns = [f'emb_{i}' for i in features_wide.columns]\n","print(f\"Después: {features_wide.shape} (nodos × dimensiones)\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":36,"status":"ok","timestamp":1747228585214,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"},"user_tz":300},"id":"1HK_JE0UmpUl","outputId":"479a3664-d890-4e2f-844d-5bbb8a1d7ba3"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Antes: (37700, 3) filas de target\n","Después: (37700, 1) (nodos × etiqueta)\n"]}],"source":["# 3) target_df: renombrar, eliminar name y duplicados\n","target_df = pd.read_csv('musae_git_target.csv')\n","print(f\"Antes: {target_df.shape} filas de target\")\n","target_df = (\n","    target_df\n","    .drop(columns=['name'])\n","    .drop_duplicates(subset='id')\n","    .rename(columns={'ml_target':'label'})\n","    .set_index('id')\n",")\n","print(f\"Después: {target_df.shape} (nodos × etiqueta)\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":36,"status":"ok","timestamp":1747228585327,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"},"user_tz":300},"id":"EbhdOVd3mvTW","outputId":"216257dc-3a80-4764-e355-66dbd89fe3ed"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Nodos comunes a los 3 datasets: 37700\n"]}],"source":["# 4) Verificar integridad: nodos comunes entre los tres\n","nodes_edges   = set(edges_df['id_1']).union(edges_df['id_2'])\n","nodes_feat    = set(features_wide.index)\n","nodes_target  = set(target_df.index)\n","common_nodes  = nodes_edges & nodes_feat & nodes_target\n","print(f\"Nodos comunes a los 3 datasets: {len(common_nodes)}\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"Q1QWfnxzro58"},"source":["#implementaciones del proyecto\n","# Plan de trabajo (CRISP-DM)\n","\n","1. **Acceso y descripción de datos**  \n","   - Cargar `musae_git_edges.csv`, `musae_git_features.csv` y `musae_git_target.csv`.  \n","   - Reportar número de nodos y aristas en la red social (sin graficar).\n","\n","2. **Extracción de features topológicos**  \n","   - Construir grafo dirigido con NetworkX.  \n","   - Calcular métricas de centralidad: degree, in_degree, out_degree, degree_centrality, betweenness, closeness, eigenvector, pagerank, clustering, average_neighbor_degree.\n","\n","3. **Extracción de métricas de enlace**  \n","   - Limitar candidatos (aristas existentes + muestras negativas de segundo orden).  \n","   - Calcular common_neighbors, jaccard, adamic_adar, preferential_attachment para cada par.  \n","   - Agregar al perfil de cada nodo (promedio por nodo).\n","\n","4. **Limpieza e integración independiente**  \n","   - **Edges**: eliminar duplicados y self-loops.  \n","   - **Features**: pivotar `(node, feature)` a columnas `emb_0, emb_1, …`.  \n","   - **Target**: renombrar `ml_target` a `label`, eliminar `name`, y poner `id` como índice.\n","\n","5. **Merge final y filtrado de nodos comunes**  \n","   - Unir métricas topológicas, métricas de enlace, embeddings y etiquetas por `id`.  \n","   - Filtrar solo nodos presentes en las 4 fuentes.\n","\n","6. **Split 60-20-20**  \n","   - Dividir `full_df` en `X_train (60%)`, `X_val (20%)`, `X_test (20%)`, estratificado por `label`.\n","\n","7. **Modelado y optimización**  \n","   - Entrenar al menos 2 clasificadores: LinearSVC y XGBoost.  \n","   - Optimizar hiperparámetros con `GridSearchCV` (scoring='roc_auc').\n","\n","8. **Selección de mejor modelo**  \n","   - Comparar métricas (ROC-AUC, F1, precisión, recall) en selección del conjunto de validación.\n","\n","9. **Evaluación final en test**  \n","   - Aplicar el mejor modelo a `X_test` y reportar métricas de calidad.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"YVcacTcortYM"},"source":["##Cálculo de métricas de centralidad para cada nodo"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":3067,"status":"ok","timestamp":1747229009590,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"},"user_tz":300},"id":"AkRkdPDjrwgM","outputId":"d072f0d2-5c6a-4fde-c116-b7f5c0470255"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Requirement already satisfied: python-igraph in /usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages (0.11.8)\n","Requirement already satisfied: igraph==0.11.8 in /usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages (from python-igraph) (0.11.8)\n","Requirement already satisfied: texttable>=1.6.2 in /usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages (from igraph==0.11.8->python-igraph) (1.7.0)\n"]}],"source":["# Celda 0.1: Instalar python-igraph en Colab\n","!pip install python-igraph\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"VTx7k-x7vJeI"},"source":["## Caracteriza a cada nodo a partir de métricas adecuadas (métricas asociadas al grafo). Emplea la mayor cantidad de métricas para asegurarte de caractaerizar de la mejro manera a los nodos."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"77Iakgw7vM9Z"},"source":["# Predicción de enlaces\n","\n","Dado un par de nodos, $A$ y $B$ (**no conectados**), buscamos predecir si en el futuro ambos estarán conectados. Podemos usar como predictores diferentes medidas que caracterizan a ambos nodos algunas de las cuales se discutirán en este documento.\n","\n","\n","## Vecinos comunes\n","\n","\n","$$\\text{comm_neigh}(A, B) = |N(A)\\cap N(B)|$$"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"executionInfo":{"elapsed":117666,"status":"ok","timestamp":1747229455194,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"},"user_tz":300},"id":"HvIhr_4k6_Cg","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"outputId":"34112f58-2f37-4d82-8e44-89cbb37a2c93"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Graph is not strongly connected. Calculating eigenvector centrality per SCC.\n"]}],"source":["# Celda 1: Extracción optimizada de métricas topológicas (genera metrics_df)\n","import pandas as pd\n","import networkx as nx\n","\n","# Cambiar la ruta del archivo a la ruta relativa\n","edges_df = pd.read_csv('musae_git_edges.csv', names=['id_1','id_2'], header=0)\n","G = nx.from_pandas_edgelist(edges_df, 'id_1', 'id_2', create_using=nx.DiGraph())\n","\n","in_degree  = dict(G.in_degree())\n","out_degree = dict(G.out_degree())\n","degree     = dict(G.degree())\n","deg_cent   = nx.degree_centrality(G)\n","betw_cent  = nx.betweenness_centrality(G, k=500, normalized=True, seed=42)\n","\n","# --- Manejar eigenvector centrality for disconnected graphs ---\n","eig_cent = {} # Initialize an empty dictionary for eigenvector centrality\n","if nx.is_strongly_connected(G):\n","    # If strongly connected, calculate directly\n","    eig_cent = nx.eigenvector_centrality_numpy(G)\n","else:\n","    # If not strongly connected, calculate for each strongly connected component (SCC)\n","    print(\"Graph is not strongly connected. Calculating eigenvector centrality per SCC.\")\n","    for component in nx.strongly_connected_components(G):\n","        subgraph = G.subgraph(component)\n","        if len(subgraph) > 1: # Eigenvector centrality is meaningful for components > 1 node\n","            try:\n","                # Calculate centrality for the subgraph\n","                sub_eig_cent = nx.eigenvector_centrality_numpy(subgraph)\n","                # Merge the results back into the main dictionary\n","                eig_cent.update(sub_eig_cent)\n","            except Exception as e:\n","                # Handle potential errors within a component, e.g., if a component still causes issues\n","                print(f\"Could not calculate eigenvector centrality for a component: {e}\")\n","        else:\n","             # For single-node components, centrality is undefined or zero\n","             node = list(component)[0]\n","             eig_cent[node] = 0.0 # Assign 0 or a small value\n","\n","pagerank   = nx.pagerank(G)\n","clust      = nx.clustering(G.to_undirected())\n","avg_nb_deg = nx.average_neighbor_degree(G)\n","\n","metrics_df = pd.DataFrame({\n","    'in_degree': pd.Series(in_degree),\n","    'out_degree': pd.Series(out_degree),\n","    'degree': pd.Series(degree),\n","    'degree_cent': pd.Series(deg_cent),\n","    'betweenness': pd.Series(betw_cent),\n","    'eigenvector_nx': pd.Series(eig_cent), # Use the potentially component-wise calculated dict\n","    'pagerank': pd.Series(pagerank),\n","    'clustering': pd.Series(clust),\n","    'avg_nb_degree': pd.Series(avg_nb_deg),\n","})"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":19691,"status":"ok","timestamp":1747229700273,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"},"user_tz":300},"id":"Bfhy-3Lo7XaA","outputId":"83b711c4-0057-4644-865c-54227fc43067"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Common Neighbors: [((0, 23977), 0), ((1, 34526), 0), ((1, 2370), 1), ((1, 14683), 1), ((1, 29982), 3)]\n","Jaccard: [((0, 23977), 0.0), ((1, 34526), 0.0), ((1, 2370), 0.02127659574468085), ((1, 14683), 0.008849557522123894), ((1, 29982), 0.006072874493927126)]\n","Adamic–Adar: [((0, 23977), 0), ((1, 34526), 0), ((1, 2370), 0.1614892541739433), ((1, 14683), 0.15301653887445435), ((1, 29982), 0.5906603320417773)]\n","Pref. Attach.: [((0, 23977), 32), ((1, 34526), 16), ((1, 2370), 320), ((1, 14683), 848), ((1, 29982), 3912)]\n"]}],"source":["# Define ebunch using the existing edges\n","ebunch = list(edges_df.itertuples(index=False, name=None))\n","\n","# ————— 1) Precomputar vecinos como conjuntos (en grafo no dirigido) —————\n","# Moved this section before the loop\n","U = G.to_undirected()\n","neighbors = {n: set(U.neighbors(n)) for n in U.nodes()}\n","\n","# Now you can proceed to calculate link prediction metrics for these pairs\n","# ————— 3) Calcular métricas de enlace solo para ebunch usando sets —————\n","import math\n","\n","cn_scores = {}\n","jacc_scores = {}\n","aa_scores = {}\n","pa_scores = {}\n","\n","for u, v in ebunch:\n","    # Asegúrate de que u y v existen como keys en neighbors\n","    # aunque para las aristas existentes deberían estar.\n","    # Puedes añadir un check si es necesario:\n","    if u in neighbors and v in neighbors:\n","        Nu = neighbors[u]\n","        Nv = neighbors[v]\n","        inter = Nu & Nv\n","        union = Nu | Nv\n","\n","        cn_scores[(u, v)] = len(inter)\n","        jacc_scores[(u, v)] = len(inter) / len(union) if union else 0.0\n","        # Adamic-Adar: ensure neighbors[w] > 1 to avoid log(1)\n","        aa_scores[(u, v)] = sum(1 / math.log(len(neighbors[w]))\n","                                for w in inter\n","                                if w in neighbors and len(neighbors[w]) > 1)\n","        pa_scores[(u, v)] = len(Nu) * len(Nv)\n","    else:\n","        # Optional: handle cases where u or v are not in the neighbors dict\n","        # This might happen if ebunch includes nodes not present in the graph\n","        print(f\"Warning: Node(s) {u} or {v} not found in graph for ebunch pair.\")\n","\n","\n","# Ejemplo: ver primeras 5 puntuaciones\n","print(\"Common Neighbors:\", list(cn_scores.items())[:5])\n","print(\"Jaccard:\", list(jacc_scores.items())[:5])\n","print(\"Adamic–Adar:\", list(aa_scores.items())[:5])\n","print(\"Pref. Attach.:\", list(pa_scores.items())[:5])"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"IFdIXiLBvTPp"},"source":["# Coeficiente de Jaccard\n","\n","$$\\text{jacc_coeff}(A, B) = \\frac{|N(A)\\cap N(B)|}{|N(A)\\cup N(B)|}$$"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":4172,"status":"ok","timestamp":1747229708271,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"},"user_tz":300},"id":"B1bpRYYq70oq","outputId":"e98f034c-20ee-4b08-fa8e-2b106723f476"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["(0, 23977): 0.0000\n","(1, 34526): 0.0000\n","(1, 2370): 0.0213\n","(1, 14683): 0.0088\n","(1, 29982): 0.0061\n"]}],"source":["# ————— 1) Precomputar vecinos como conjuntos (en grafo no dirigido) —————\n","U = G.to_undirected()\n","neighbors = {n: set(U.neighbors(n)) for n in U.nodes()}\n","\n","# ————— 2) Definir ebunch (por ejemplo, aristas existentes + muestras negativas) —————\n","# ya deberías tenerlo en una lista `ebunch`\n","\n","# ————— 3) Cálculo manual y rápido de Jaccard —————\n","jacc_scores = {}\n","for u, v in ebunch:\n","    Nu, Nv = neighbors[u], neighbors[v]\n","    inter_size = len(Nu & Nv)\n","    # |union| = |Nu| + |Nv| - |intersection|\n","    union_size = len(Nu) + len(Nv) - inter_size\n","    jacc_scores[(u, v)] = inter_size / union_size if union_size else 0.0\n","\n","# ————— 4) Ejemplo de salida —————\n","for pair, score in list(jacc_scores.items())[:5]:\n","    print(f\"{pair}: {score:.4f}\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"LOtwFl1AvYHy"},"source":["## Índice Adamic-Adar\n","\n","$$\\text{adamic}(A, B) = \\sum_{u \\in N(A)\\cap N(B)}\\frac{1}{log|N(u)|}$$\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":2676,"status":"ok","timestamp":1747229713243,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","